    {
      "id": 130808,
      "name": "phantaskippy",
      "username": "phantaskippy",
      "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/phantaskippy/{size}/1897_2.png",
      "created_at": "2015-02-07T21:07:00.000Z",
      "cooked": "<p>Characters do not block line of sight, only elevation can do that.</p><p>Further, Omnitron is treated as 1 elevation higher than the hex he is on.</p><p>This means the elevation increase for Omnitron being in the hex is for the character only, not the hex, which mean a character moving through a hex Omnitron occupies does not account for Omnitron's increased height for movement cost.</p><p>The Elevation of the Hex is not raised, only the Character of Omniron-V.</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>By rule Omnitron-V cannot block line of sight, even if he is treated as one elevation higher than the hex he is on.</p>",
      "post_number": 3,
      "post_type": 1,
      "updated_at": "2021-02-07T04:05:59.765Z",
      "reply_count": 0,
      "reply_to_post_number": null,
      "quote_count": 0,
      "incoming_link_count": 0,
